
# Story: X.402 Testnet Payment — Unlock Full Code Review

**Slug:** `payment-x402` | **Status:** Draft  
**Issue:** #ISSUE_NUMBER | **Team:** Yellow

---

## Summary

This story implements a testnet X.402 payment flow that unlocks a full C++ code review previously shown as a partial teaser in chat. The flow must be secure, idempotent, server-verified, and produce a verifiable receipt stored in the vault.

---

## User Story

> As a Technical Manager (ICP) who received a partial C++ code review teaser in the chat, I want to complete an X.402 testnet payment from a web payment portal (providing my wallet info and optionally uploading my codebase), so that once the transaction is confirmed the full review is delivered into a secure vault only I can access and I receive a verifiable receipt as proof of purchase.

---

## Acceptance Criteria

**AC-1 (UI):** Given the user clicks "Request Full Review" in chat, When the payment flow opens, Then the UI shows a payment modal/portal with: amount, currency label `TESTNET`, a payment URI and QR fallback, wallet copy instructions, TTL countdown, and a visible "I paid" action.

**AC-2 (persistence):** Given a payment request is issued, When the backend creates a PaymentRequest, Then the Firestore document stores: id, amount, currency, generated walletAddress/paymentURI, status=`pending`, createdAt, expiresAt (TTL), and codeReviewId.

**AC-3 (verification):** Given the user sends funds on-testnet, When the server verifies the tx (txHash or webhook), Then PaymentRequest.status → `confirmed`, CodeReview.paid → `true`, and a Receipt is created and linked to the CodeReview; the vault gets the full review and access is restricted to the purchaser.

**AC-4 (errors):** Given payment fails, is invalid, or TTL expires, When the user attempts to unlock the review, Then the UI shows a clear error with retry instructions and contact support; no review is unlocked.

**AC-5 (idempotency):** Given duplicate tx notifications or retries, When backend processes them, Then processing is idempotent: no double-credit, receipts remain unique, and subsequent notifications are no-ops.

**AC-6 (security):** Given front-end and back-end components, When implementing the flow, Then no secrets are committed; verification uses env-backed credentials and server-side logic only.

