## Technical Approach

- UI
  - `src/components/Payment.tsx` — presentational payment modal/portal. Must render all fields server-provided (amount, currency, walletAddress/paymentURI, QR fallback, TTL, copy button, "I paid" button). Provide a non-JS fallback anchor with the payment URI for high-latency clients.
  - `src/app/payment/page.tsx` — route for full portal that also accepts a file-upload component for the codebase (optional) and basic wallet metadata input. This page is reachable from the chat CTA.
- Backend / Agents (server-side)
  - `src/agents/payments.ts` — server-only helpers (createPaymentRequest, verifyTransaction, handleWebhook, markConfirmed). These run in secure environment (Cloud Function / server endpoint).
  - Firestore collections: `paymentRequests`, `receipts`. Follow data model in `docs/agent/data-model.md`.
  - Verification is performed via a testnet provider (RPC or block-explorer API). Do verification server-side only; accept webhooks for efficiency and/or periodic polling for confirmation.
  - On confirmation: set PaymentRequest.status = `confirmed`, set codeReview.paid = true, persist receipt, and trigger storing full review into user's vault (vault access control enforced server-side).
- Constraints
  - Testnet only in preview/dev.
  - Do not commit private keys or provider credentials. Provide placeholders in `.env.example`.
  - TypeScript strict mode enforced; no any/ts-ignore.
  - Keep the UI accessible (keyboard, screen-readers) and performant.

