## Test Plan (Vitest + React Testing Library + unit tests for backend logic)

Write tests with Given/When/Then names matching ACs.

UI tests (Vitest + RTL)
- "Given a user opens the payment modal, When it renders, Then amount, TESTNET label, walletAddress/paymentURI, QR fallback, TTL, and 'I paid' are visible"
- "Given JS is disabled, When the portal loads, Then the payment URI anchor is present and navigable"

Backend unit tests
- "Given a code review needs payment, When createPaymentRequest is called, Then a pending PaymentRequest is persisted with correct TTL and fields"
- "Given a pending PaymentRequest and a valid txHash, When verifyTransaction runs, Then PaymentRequest becomes 'confirmed', CodeReview.paid = true, and a Receipt is created"
- "Given duplicate tx notifications, When processed twice, Then only one Receipt is created and state remains consistent"
- "Given a payment that expires, When TTL elapses, Then PaymentRequest.status becomes 'expired' and no review is unlocked"

Integration / End-to-end (mock provider)
- Simulate full flow: create request → simulate tx broadcast → webhook/poll verification → confirm → assert vault contains full review and receipt exists

Manual verification
- Deploy to preview, use a testnet wallet, complete a tx, verify receipt issuance and vault access.

